cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Smallest witnesses by girth for rad(n) | f(n)"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Ellena Godoy"
    given-names: "Jorge"
abstract: >-
  For a multiplicative function f, let S(f) be the set of integers n with
  rad(n) dividing f(n), and let the covering digraph of n have the primes
  dividing n as vertices with an edge q -> p whenever p divides f(q^e), where
  q^e is the exact power of q in n. This work computes the smallest member of
  S(f) of each girth, for f = sigma, sigma* and phi*, and proves that any such
  minimal witness of girth k has exactly k distinct prime factors and a covering
  digraph that is a pure directed cycle. That theorem turns the search into the
  construction of cycles over small primes, which yields three values beyond the
  reach of exhaustive search, the largest near 4.5e12. All results are verified
  by two independent implementations and cross-checked against the count of
  prime-abundant numbers published by Pollack and Pomerance (2012).
keywords:
  - number theory
  - arithmetic functions
  - sum of divisors
  - prime-abundant numbers
  - covering digraph
  - girth
  - integer sequences
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-03"
references:
